{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #19 — e369 + parity 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #18 (+ its 3 ADDENDA), THEN #17. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family. ALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"\nCLOSES from a worktree whose HEAD CONTAINS the commits (/Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag, needs\n`git merge --ff-only gerrit/main` first). `--ref` does NOT satisfy the file_impact precheck.\nDO NOT trust the board below — read the tickets.\n\n*** THE HEADLINE: A HARNESS RUN CONTRADICTED A FIX THAT WAS ALREADY MERGED. ***\nRun **30784592232** (main @ de2f1ed87): `[jira-live-canary] collected=56 executed=56 skipped=0`,\n**4 failed / 52 passed**, 23m36s. Every failure carried information:\n 1. **751e VERIFIED LIVE** — `test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` PASSED. Its fix (205935bd72) works.\n 2. **`test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips` STILL RED even though 2b16's fix is MERGED.** See below —\n    the cause is an error in MY PLAN, not in the implementation. **This blocks e369.**\n 3. **`test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` → `SETUP FAILED`: Data Center REFUSES to null a sub-task's\n    `fields.parent`** — HTTP 400 `{\"errors\":{\"parent\":\"data was not an object\"}}`. **THIS SETTLES THE\n    PLATFORM UNKNOWN that 5200 and 88d9 both carried.** A sub-task exists only under a parent, so nulling\n    it may not be a legal DC edit at all. 88d9's AC already anticipates this branch: the cell reporting\n    SETUP FAILED is a PLATFORM finding, NOT 88d9 failing. Do not \"fix\" the cell.\n 4. **`test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips` RED — LIVE CONFIRMATION of [rebar:39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b].**\n    The local parent was detached; DC still carries `fields.parent`. 39c1 was filed off a CODE READING\n    (disjoint emit/apply gates); it is now an observed defect.\n 5. `test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips` — `get_parent_map never reflected the reparent within\n    90s (45 attempts)`. The cell says explicitly this is NOT a bridge defect (search-index lag, or the map\n    read degraded to `{}` per its own contract). Treat as harness/index timing, not product.\n\n*** 2b16: THE FIX IS MERGED AND DOES NOT WORK. THE PLAN I WROTE WAS WRONG. ***\nLanded G4 (`inbound_differ.py:754-781`) drops an inbound `remove` whenever outbound has that target in\n`link_add_keys`. My stated reasoning was \"an outbound ADD means 'being pushed', NOT 'peer deleted it'\".\n**That inference fails TOTALLY:** when the peer deletes a link, the local dep still exists and the peer\nlacks it — which is precisely when outbound emits an ADD. So G4 suppresses EVERY legitimate\npeer-deletion mirror and the feature can never fire in a bidirectional pass.\nIts mutation ledger is green because `test_g4_outbound_add_this_pass_suppresses_the_removal` asserts the\nbehaviour I specified. **A green mutation ledger cannot catch a wrong SPECIFICATION** — only the live\noracle did. Carry that: mutation-proof means \"the code does what the plan says\", not \"the plan is right\".\n\n**THE CORRECTED RULE — `managed_refs` decides PRECEDENCE; it is not a second AND-gate beside G4:**\n  * ref IS managed (we pushed it once) + peer lacks it → **the peer deleted it** → inbound REMOVE wins,\n    and **the outbound ADD for that pair must be suppressed too.**\n  * ref NOT managed (never pushed) + peer lacks it → we just have not pushed it → outbound ADD wins,\n    suppress the inbound REMOVE. (This is the ONLY case G4 should cover.)\n**Scope consequence: `outbound_links.py` (or the shared suppression context) JOINS the file impact.**\nSuppressing only inbound leaves the pass divergent — inbound unlinks locally while outbound re-adds in\nJira, and the next pass re-adopts it. Churn, not convergence. This is arbitration across BOTH differs,\nwhich the original plan never contemplated.\nChange 1276 is NOT being reverted: the removal differ, the apply-layer action branch + `rebar.unlink`\nwiring, and G1/G2/G3/G5 are correct and independently mutation-proven, and the apply-layer drop it fixed\nwas a real defect. Only the arbitration is wrong. Residual risk after the correction:\n`seed_managed_refs_from_current` marks a pre-feature ticket's CURRENT deps as managed, so a never-pushed\ndep there could read as \"peer deleted\" — narrower than \"never works\", but record it.\n\n*** 88d9: IMPLEMENTED AND GREEN, NOT VERIFIED, NOT PUSHED. TWO AGENTS STALLED ON IT. ***\n`/Users/joeoakhart/wt-88d9`, branch `fix-88d9-inbound-parent-clear`, base de2f1ed87, **working tree CLEAN**,\ntwo WIP commits: `1b28b9c85 WIP: RED...` (fetcher.py + the 506-line test module) and `8d727fbc7 WIP: layer\n2 green` (inbound_differ.py + inbound_fields.py). `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/` → **287 passed**\n(271 before + 16 new). LOC: **inbound_differ.py 797 → 773 (NET NEGATIVE — the extraction into\ninbound_fields.py worked), inbound_fields.py 247 → 351, fetcher.py 670 → 707.** All under the 800 cap.\nByte-verified backups of the FIXED files are in **`/tmp/88d9-bak/`** — use those to restore after each\nmutation (`git restore --source=HEAD <file>` also works; NEVER `git checkout -- <file>`).\nSTILL TO DO: the mutation ledger (incl. an UNCONDITIONAL-CLEAR mutation), the end-to-end proof\n(differ → payload → apply → reduced ticket `parent_id` empty), the snapshot-`parent`-consumer sweep, then\nsquash to ONE commit and push. **Two agents stalled here (watchdog, 600s no progress) — do the ledger\nINLINE/scripted rather than dispatching a third.**\n\n*** 5200 STACK: 1279 + 1280 MERGED (4bbbdd991, a1037d020). 1283 at Verified -1. ***\n1283's -1 was SELF-INFLICTED and is a new trap instance: my queued `recheck-review` on it ALSO triggered\nCI (the substring trap in ADDENDUM 3), two overlapping runs cancelled each other, and the `if: always()`\nvote job voted -1 off the CANCELLED one. The surviving run then failed only `golden-path (clean install)`\n— on a TEST-ONLY change, so almost certainly transient. A plain **`recheck`** (CI only, no LLM churn) has\nbeen posted. **On a stack, never fire `recheck-review` while anything else is in flight.**\nAlso observed: the LLM review bot CATCHES UP on its own — 1283 and then 1279 both got their votes without\nfurther prodding, after appearing to have been skipped. Prefer patience over churn.\n\n--- WHAT REMAINS TO CLOSE e369 ---\n 1. **2b16** — amend the plan to the corrected precedence rule, widen file impact to include\n    `outbound_links.py`, re-run `review-plan`, implement, land, re-run the harness, close.\n 2. **88d9** — finish the ledger + push + land. Its live cell may legitimately end at `SETUP FAILED`\n    (finding 3 above); that satisfies its AC's platform branch.\n 3. **5200** — land 1283, re-run the harness, then tick its 18 ACs (verification already recorded on the\n    ticket) and close.\n 4. **e369** — its plan review is `stale-code`; re-run it. Its 13 ACs are verified: 11 MET, AC1 BLOCKED on\n    the three children, AC5 already AMENDED. Then close.\n Consider whether finding 4 (39c1 confirmed LIVE) changes the operator's non-gating ruling — it was filed\n as BORDERLINE precisely because, unlike e39f, it does not fail safe. It is now observed, not theoretical."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785768157478628001,"uuid":"4c5b726d-5288-478c-af2d-0f596685036b"}